{"id":"u-5fab7e32-7105-46ff-9640-e634021646b9","src":"community","title":"Personal 4 Weeks Beginner Olympic Weightlifting","author":"Daru","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/BYn5aL-personal-4-weeks-beginner-olympic-weightlifting","desc":"Short microcycle program for beginners that you can repeat continuously. You can have no deload weeks, though it is recommended to have one . Each week increases either volume, intensity, or both.\n\nDay 1: Snatch + Front Squat \nDay 2: Clean & Jerk + Back Squat\nDay 3: Power variations + overhead strength\nDay 4: Heavy Snatch, Clean & Jerk + Front Squat\n\nDon't automatically increase weight on every lift at the end of the cycle. Only increase the 1RM% when you are sure that you can handle the previous cycle.\n\nRecommended warmups for each days:\nMonday – Snatch\nCardio 2m, wrist rocks 30s, ankle rocks 12/side, world's greatest stretch 5/side, deep squat hold 45s, thoracic rotations 8/side, Lu raises 5lb 2×12, OHS 2×8, muscle snatch 2×5.\n\nTuesday – Clean & Jerk\nCardio 2m, wrist rocks 30s, ankle rocks 12/side, world's greatest stretch 5/side, deep squat hold 45s, thoracic rotations 8/side, Lu raises 5lb 2×12, front squat 2×5, strict press 1×8, front rack stretch 30s.\n\nThursday – Power Variations\nCardio 2m, arm circles 15 each direction, leg swings 10 each direction/leg, world's greatest stretch 5/side, ankle rocks 10/side, thoracic rotations 8/side, Lu raises 5lb 2×12, muscle snatch 2×5, muscle clean 2×5, push press 2×5.\n\nSaturday – Heavy Singles\nCardio 2m, wrist rocks 30s, ankle rocks 12/side, world's greatest stretch 5/side, deep squat hold 45s, thoracic rotations 8/side, Lu raises 5lb 2×12, OHS 1×8, front squat 1×5, muscle snatch 1×5, muscle clean 1×5.","level":["Beginner","Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Olympic Weightlifting","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":120,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-11-03T04:20:29.198Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Snatch + Front Squat","C